sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch13-03> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-03--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-03--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch13-03: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.55" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.545"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.58"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Constancy and deep phylogenetic signal are measurable, but the adaptive status of a character is not a standard column and has to be assigned. Existing matrices and trait databases support the comparison in scattered taxa, especially vertebrates and some plant families. Harmonizing those matrices and coding function would take months, and the coding step limits how decisive the result can be." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: In morphological matrices, partition characters into those tied to special habits and those that are structural, then compare their constancy across large clades and their phylogenetic signal at deep nodes. The claim is confirmed if habit-linked characters are less conserved and less informative for higher groups, and refuted if they are as constant as, or more constant than, structural characters." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Deciding that a character has been 'little modified by adaptation' is itself an interpretation and will differ among coders.", "Systematists already prefer constant characters, so high classificatory value is partly how the matrices were assembled.", "Public matrices cover a minority of animal and plant groups, with a strong bias toward vertebrates." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-03--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-03--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-03--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-03--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch13-03 by Grok 4.7: 0.6" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.6"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-03--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch13-03> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-03--grok--operationalizability> .
